  "prompt_text": "The figure is a broad overview of how altermagnetic or spin-based materials could be used across several device platforms. On the left, a spintronics schematic shows a multilayer memory/logic architecture with two logic states, “1” and “0,” represented by opposite spin directions. Arrows indicate two main application directions: ultrafast THz oscillators and gated spin logic devices. A text box highlights likely technologies such as MRAM, spin field-effect transistors, neuromorphic computing, and THz nano-oscillators.\n\nThe right side expands this into a wider materials and device landscape. In photonics, a pump–probe setup suggests optical control and readout of ultrafast spin dynamics at THz frequencies. In magnonics, spin waves propagate through a patterned structure, emphasizing magnon band splitting and magnon-current transport. In phononics, a surface acoustic wave device modulates the material dynamically. Multiferrroicity is represented by electric-field control of a layered structure, implying electrical manipulation of magnetic order. Superconductivity is linked to unusual paired-state transport effects, and topology is illustrated by edge-like circulating states, suggesting quantum anomalous Hall behavior and related topological semimetal physics. Overall, the figure presents one magnetic platform as a hub for ultrafast, wave-based, electrically tunable, superconducting, and topological functionalities.",
